    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Tucked away on a neat, secluded, and gated backwater site originally forming part of the rear garden of No. 10 Station Road, Cush Lodge is a hidden gem. Occupying a peaceful, almost rural setting on a generous c0.3 acre  site, this unique property directly overlooks the picturesque 5th green of Sutton Golf Club.\r\n\r\nDespite this remarkably quiet and private backdrop, the house offers exceptional convenience, situated just a short stroll from the bustling hub of Sutton Cross, local beaches, and transport links.\r\n\r\nBuilt approximately 50 years ago, Cush Lodge is a home where comfort, warmth, and a genuinely homely atmosphere take centre stage. It has been designed to offer an easy, manageable lifestyle without compromising on character or a sense of space. The accommodation is mostly single-storey, thoughtfully laid out to be both modest and highly functional.\r\n\r\nAt its heart is an intimate dining area and a comfortable kitchen/breakfast room that serves as a welcoming hub for daily life. The bedrooms are well-proportioned, perfect for a family and/or visiting guests. The main living room is a truly special space, featuring large picture windows that frame the shifting light and exceptional views over the golf course. Upstairs, a unique mezzanine space opens onto a private balcony, offering a quiet retreat with a captivating vantage point and access to a practical, floored walk-in attic space.\r\n\r\nFor those looking to trade down from a larger family home in the locality, Cush Lodge represents the perfect retirement haven. It retains the independent space of a detached home and a beautifully established garden, while providing a highly accessible layout that is easy to maintain, with excellent scope for affordable BER energy alignment.\r\n\r\nOutside, the surprisingly generous private gardens offer a secluded sanctuary for anyone with a passion for gardening. The mature, landscaped gardens have previously featured as a Horticultural Society show garden, boasting lawns to both the front and rear, vibrant herbaceous borders, a glasshouse, a garden shed, and raised beds ready for cultivation.\r\n\r\nCush Lodge offers a rare combination of complete privacy, soothing views, and absolute convenience to Sutton’s amenities. It is a warm, inviting home ready for its very fortunate new owners.\r\n\r\nViewing is available by appointment with Gallagher Quigley\r\n\r\nTel: 01 818 3000 | Email: info@gallagherquigley.ie"
      },
